%U A400359 8,4,6,5,1,2,8,0,3,9,4,5,4,8,0,7,0,8,6,2,5,6
%N A400359 Decimal expansion of 9 - 5*sqrt(3) - 7*sqrt(6)/2 + 6*sqrt(2).
%C A400359 Largest possible minimal pairwise distance of thirteen points inside an equilateral triangle with unit side length.
%C A400359 Equivalently, largest diameter of the circles in the densest packing of thirteen equal circles inside an equilateral triangle with side length equal to 1 + sqrt(3)*(this constant). If the circles had unit radius, the corresponding triangle would have side length A399816.
%C A400359 This value was conjectured by Melissen (1993) and later proved by Joós (2021). See also Tedeschi (2021).
%H A400359 Paolo Xausa, <a href="/A400359/b400359.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 0..10000</a>
%H A400359 Antal Joós, <a href="https://doi.org/10.1007/s00010-020-00753-y">Packing 13 circles in an equilateral triangle</a>, Aequat. Math. 95, pp. 35-65 (2021).
%H A400359 Hans (J. B. M.) Melissen, <a href="https://doi.org/10.2307/2324212">Densest Packings of Congruent Circles in an Equilateral Triangle</a>, The American Mathematical Monthly, Vol. 100, Issue 10 (1993), pp. 916-925 (also available on <a href="https://www.jstor.org/stable/2324212">JSTOR</a>).
%H A400359 Natalie Tedeschi, <a href="https://doi.org/10.33697/ajur.2021.042">On Packing Thirteen Points in an Equilateral Triangle</a>, American Journal of Undergraduate Research, Volume 18, Issue 2, September 2021.
%H A400359 Wikipedia, <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Circle_packing_in_an_equilateral_triangle">Circle packing in an equilateral triangle</a>.
%H A400359 <a href="/index/Al#algebraic_04">Index entries for algebraic numbers, degree 4</a>.
%F A400359 Equals 9 - 5*A002194 - 7*A115754 + A010524.
%F A400359 Equals 2/(A399816 - 2*A002194).
%F A400359 Equals the smallest root of 4*x^4 - 144*x^3 + 180*x^2 - 72*x + 9.
%e A400359 0.2518132366530604814824063762582067648231888009114...
%t A400359 First[RealDigits[9 - Sqrt[75] - 7*Sqrt[6]/2 + Sqrt[72], 10, 100]]
%Y A400359 Analogous values for k points: 1 (k = 2, 3), A020760 (k = 4), A020761 (k = 5, 6), A152422 (k = 7), A400357 (k = 8), A010701 (k = 9, 10), A400358 (k = 11), A019913 (k = 12), A020773 (k = 14, 15).
